EXPERIMENT 39 – CONTROLLING TEST FLOW USING LOOP, ONCE ONLY AND IF CONTROLLERS IN APACHE JMETER
AIM
To use Apache JMeter to control the flow of a test plan using the Loop, Once Only and If controllers.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and rename the Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Add User Defined Variables with variable run = yes.
4. Set Number of Threads = 1 and Loop Count = 2.
5. Add a Once Only Controller with HTTP Request GET /login inside it. It runs only in the first iteration.
6. Add a Loop Controller with Loop Count = 3 and HTTP Request GET /checkboxes.
7. Add an If Controller with condition ${__jexl3("${run}" == "yes")} and HTTP Request GET /dropdown.
8. Add Summary Report and run the plan.
9. Change run to no and run again to verify that the If Controller skips its request.
INPUT – TEST PLAN CONFIGURATION
Element	Property	Value
User Defined Variables	run	yes
Thread Group	Threads	1
Thread Group	Ramp-up	1 second
Thread Group	Loop Count	2
Once Only Controller	Child	GET /login
Loop Controller	Loop Count	3
Loop Controller	Child	GET /checkboxes
If Controller	Condition	${__jexl3("${run}" == "yes")}
If Controller	Interpret Condition as Variable Expression	Selected
If Controller	Child	GET /dropdown

OUTPUT
Summary Report (run = yes)
Label	Samples
/login	1
/checkboxes	6
/dropdown	2
TOTAL	9

With run = no, the /dropdown request is skipped and the total becomes 7.
RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to control the flow of a test plan using the Loop, Once Only and If controllers, and the results were verified.
